TYPES.md §13.2, DECISIONS 334: a later union alternative that is not a string literal, parenthesised
or not, is a type, E3028, naming it with each literal inside read as a String: an optional literal
(`"x"?`, `("x")?`), a list of one, a map keyed by one. A nested union's first alternative is a
type again: `("a" | "b")` is E3002 for the literal in its A place only (TYPES.md §1).
-- a/a.canon --
package a

local type O1 = String | "x"?

local type O2 = String | ("y")?

local type L1 = String | ["z"]

local type M1 = String | {"k": Int}

local type N1 = String | ("a" | "b")
